# LF in the repository and in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is not housekeeping. A regression test byte-compares program output
# against the 2012 reference outputs under fortran/sample-output/ on Linux,
# macOS and Windows. A Windows checkout under core.autocrlf once checked
# mobcal_He.f out at 90,793 bytes against an 88,015-byte blob.
#
# Pinning the checkout is only half of it: gfortran's Windows runtime opens
# the output unit in text mode and the program writes CRLF there. A test
# strips end-of-line CR itself and does not rely on git having done it.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.f    text eol=lf
*.mfj  text eol=lf
*.in   text eol=lf
*.out  text eol=lf
